ed @20:26; binary built @20:33 — clean linear timeline (extract→edit→tar→build), no other touches. `env.go` comment is explicit first-party confirmation:\n&gt; \"envPreferenceDirective ... It is a boolean lever ... OFF by default keeps an ordinary code search byte-identical.\"\n\n**String diff (binary-level)**: 47759 added / 45290 removed raw, 1417/1088 filtered — but **confounded**: base was built via `go install module@pseudo-version` (module-cache paths embedded per file), fixed was built locally from `eg-src/` (local absolute paths embedded). This alone churns thousands of DWARF/path-derived strings across all 264 files regardless of content. Not usable as clean signal; noted, not trusted.\n\n**Build script / history**: no dedicated build.sh in eg-src; `.bash_history` empty/unreadable. Multiple runner scripts (`eg_matrix.sh`, `eg95_run.sh`, `run_sol.sh`, etc.) reference `entire-graph-fixed` via `ENTIRE_GRAPH_BIN` only as the invocation target, no build provenance there.\n\n**VERDICT: EQUIVALENT-WHEN-GATED-OFF** (high confidence, not absolute proof). Strongest evidence: only 6/264 .go files in the actual build source were touched post-extraction, all inside `internal/cli/{search,env}.go` + `internal/sem/search.go` + new `search_preference.go`/tests, and the author's own comment in the touched `env.go` states the flag defaults off and preserves byte-identical ordinary search. Caveat: `eg-src` has no git history, so I cannot cryptographically diff its pre-edit state against upstream commit `c9641bf1c...` (the base binary's revision) — equivalence rests on internal mtime/content consistency, not a git diff against that exact SHA.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>60795</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>12</tool_uses><duration_ms>184696</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
