{"type":"frame-link","sessionId":"27642e0f-a981-4143-aea0-6f4f8cb34d37","path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/27642e0f-a981-4143-aea0-6f4f8cb34d37/scratchpad/reader-robustness.html","frameUrl":"https://claude.ai/code/artifact/e31e6ab6-5fe4-4dfc-8242-83e64fb3fca4","title":"Reader & Judge Robustness — LoCoMo and LongMemEval","timestamp":"2026-08-16T01:14:54.696Z"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-16T01:15:17.395Z","sessionId":"27642e0f-a981-4143-aea0-6f4f8cb34d37","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a4a5c4b06d3c895f6</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/fe41fb4b-5221-41ce-afce-6a9fa3dade0c/tasks/a4a5c4b06d3c895f6.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Re-score banked retrievals with a second reader and judge\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Both tasks complete. Report published: https://claude.ai/code/artifact/e31e6ab6-5fe4-4dfc-8242-83e64fb3fca4\n\n## 1. Model inventory (5 deployments, all live)\n\n| deployment | family | route | usable |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `gpt-5.6-sol` | OpenAI | `/models/chat/completions` (`azure_ai`) | yes — reader/judge A |\n| `gpt-5.6-terra` | OpenAI | same | yes — reader T |\n| `gpt-5` | OpenAI | same | yes (unused) |\n| `claude-opus-5` | Anthropic | `/anthropic/v1/messages` | yes — reader/judge B |\n| `claude-fable-5` | Anthropic | same | yes (unused) |\n\nNot blocking: cross-family readers exist. Claude needs `x-api-key`, no `temperature` (deprecated), and returns thinking blocks first.\n\n## 2. LoCoMo factorial (n=1540 paired, 0 empties, 0 judge failures everywhere)\n\n| config | reader / judge | eg | mem0 | Δ | 95% CI | b/c | p |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| baseline (banked) | sol/sol | 94.74 | 93.83 | **+0.91** | −0.19,+2.01 | 43/29 | 0.125 |\n| control re-judge | sol/sol | 94.48 | 94.03 | +0.45 | −0.65,+1.56 | 40/33 | 0.483 |\n| **(a) reader swap** | opus/sol | 96.56 | 96.69 | **−0.13** | −1.10,+0.84 | 27/29 | 0.894 |\n| (b) judge swap | sol/opus | 94.48 | 93.51 | +0.97 | −0.19,+2.08 | 46/31 | 0.110 |\n| (c) independent | opus/opus | 96.88 | 96.62 | +0.26 | −0.78,+1.23 | 32/28 | 0.699 |\n| (d) 2nd reader | terra/sol | 93.77 | 93.44 | +0.32 | −0.97,+1.62 | 52/47 | 0.688 |\n\n- **Self-grading confound REFUTED.** Judge swap reproduces the gap (+0.91→+0.97). Judge reproducibility 99.6% (±0.4pt noise) — validates my pipeline reproduces the harness.\n- **Ranking FLIPS under a different reader** (+0.91 → −0.13). Terra shrinks it to +0.32.\n- **Nothing is significant anywhere** — the baseline itself is p=0.125, CI includes zero. The flip is the collapse of an effect that was never established.\n- Mechanism: opus lifts mem0 more (+2.86) than eg (+1.82). Both contexts contained the answer; the weaker reader was the limiter.\n\n## 3. LongMemEval\n\n**Provenance of `eg_g56_lme_base` — ESTABLISHED.** Runner survives as `~/eg_matrix.sh` on mem0harness-1 (earlier grep missed it — wrong host). `runlme base 0`: plain eg, `EG_PREFERENCE_DIRECTIVE=0`, no `--user-profile`/`EG_PROFILE` (0/500 profiles vs 498/500 for the v2 run), no chrono, section-level candidates present (`session_NNNN.md:LINE`). Residual caveat: binary was a local build from a non-git tree; only 6/264 .go files touched, all in the preference path, flag-off documented as byte-identical — strong but not cryptographic.\n\n**Same-window (n=500, both arms concurrent, banked retrievals, 0 drops/empties):**\n\n| window | eg | mem0 | Δ | CI | b/c | p |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| same-window | 89.60 | 87.40 | +2.20 | −1.00,+5.40 | 40/29 | 0.228 |\n| banked cross-window | 89.40 | 87.20 | +2.20 | −1.00,+5.40 | 38/27 | 0.215 |\n\nCross-window drift was **not** moving this comparison — delta identical. eg's lead survives same-window but was never significant. By type: knowledge-update +7.69, multi-session +4.51, temporal 0.00, single-session-preference −13.33 (n=30).\n\n## Verdict\n\neg is never significantly behind on either benchmark. But the LoCoMo lead is **reader-dependent and reverses**, and no cell on either benchmark reaches significance. Publish the reader sensitivity — a reviewer running one different reader finds the flip immediately. LME same-window holds, so that objection is fully answerable.\n\nOne caught defect worth noting: a Claude thinking-block extraction bug caused a retry storm → 7 empty answers early on. Caught, fixed, all re-measured — it would have read as reader weakness.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>249666</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>153</tool_uses><duration_ms>16787141</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
