{"parentUuid":"281751cf-75ba-42e6-908e-8b10fb4c3327","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce5YR6AFH6FwYqde9BpTp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The ranking **reverses** under an opus reader: eg 96.56 vs mem0 96.69. My current draft says the direction is stable under every configuration — that is now false and has to be corrected before anything else."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":216493,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":3977,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":216493,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3977,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":216493,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":216493},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":{"cache_miss_reason":{"type":"previous_message_not_found"}}},"requestId":"req_011Ce5YR2tJh1cGsSEBipZb5","type":"assistant","uuid":"8a01ec2a-b549-43c3-a5df-9f301d81ee45","timestamp":"2026-08-16T01:15:53.410Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"fe41fb4b-5221-41ce-afce-6a9fa3dade0c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/graph-bench-results","sessionId":"27642e0f-a981-4143-aea0-6f4f8cb34d37","version":"2.1.226","gitBranch":"main","slug":"structured-meandering-origami"}
{"parentUuid":"8a01ec2a-b549-43c3-a5df-9f301d81ee45","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce5YR6AFH6FwYqde9BpTp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MGMPYzPYe2kZJYVnsspkZS","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/graph-bench-results\npython3 - <<'PY'\ns=open(\"paper-tkde.html\").read()\norig=len(s)\n\n# ---------- 1. ABSTRACT: parity + reversal, two benchmarks ----------\nold_abs = \"\"\"Evaluated on a long-conversation question-answering benchmark\nagainst six purpose-built memory systems under a shared reader, judge and retrieval budget,\nentire-graph ranks first of eight at 94.74, a margin over the strongest inference-built system that\n<b>does not reach significance</b> (+0.91, <i>p</i> = 0.125) and narrows to +0.32 under an\nindependent reader swap. We therefore claim <b>parity</b> on accuracy with inference-built memory,\nobtained at a measured <b>zero tokens</b> of index construction against 50.85 million, and a\n<b>significant</b> 2.86-point advantage (<i>p</i> = 5.7 &times; 10<sup>&minus;7</sup>) over a\nlexical baseline built at the same zero cost.</p>\"\"\"\nnew_abs = \"\"\"Evaluated on two long-conversation benchmarks against six\npurpose-built memory systems under a shared reader, judge and retrieval budget, entire-graph is\nnever significantly ahead of the strongest inference-built system and never significantly behind it:\non LoCoMo the margin is +0.91 (<i>p</i> = 0.125) and <b>reverses to &minus;0.13 under a different\nreader</b>, while on LongMemEval it is +2.20 (<i>p</i> = 0.228) in a same-window comparison. We\ntherefore claim <b>parity</b> on accuracy, obtained at a measured <b>zero tokens</b> of index\nconstruction against 50.85 million. We report the full reader &times; judge factorial that\nestablishes this, including the reversal, because a single-reader evaluation would have supported a\nstronger claim than the evidence carries.</p>\"\"\"\nassert old_abs in s; s = s.replace(old_abs, new_abs)\n\n# ---------- 2. SUMMARY OF FINDINGS ----------\nold_sum = \"\"\"<p class=\"first\">On LoCoMo [38], entire-graph ranks first of eight at 94.74. We\ndeliberately do <i>not</i> present this as an accuracy win. The margin over the strongest\ninference-built competitor is 0.91 points at <i>p</i> = 0.125, and under a full reader swap it\nnarrows to 0.32 points at <i>p</i> = 0.69. The honest reading is <i>parity</i>. What is not at\nparity is the cost of getting there: zero tokens against a measured 50.85 million, a difference that\nis an exact count rather than a statistical estimate, and which recurs on every corpus change.\nSeparately, and unlike the comparison against inference-built systems, the 2.86-point margin over a\nBM25 baseline built at identical zero cost is significant at <i>p</i> = 5.7 &times;\n10<sup>&minus;7</sup>.</p>\"\"\"\nnew_sum = \"\"\"<p class=\"first\">On LoCoMo [38], entire-graph scores 94.74 against 93.83\nfor the strongest inference-built competitor, ranking first of eight. We deliberately do <i>not</i>\npresent this as an accuracy win, and Section XII explains why in detail: the margin is 0.91 points at\n<i>p</i> = 0.125, and across a six-cell reader &times; judge factorial it ranges from +0.97 to\n<b>&minus;0.13</b>. Under one reader the ordering reverses. On LongMemEval, in a same-window\ncomparison, entire-graph leads by 2.20 points at <i>p</i> = 0.228. The honest reading across both\nbenchmarks is <i>parity</i>: never significantly ahead, never significantly behind.</p>\n\n<p>What is not at parity is the cost of getting there: zero tokens against a measured 50.85 million,\na difference that is an exact count rather than a statistical estimate, and which recurs on every\ncorpus change. Under the primary configuration the 2.86-point margin over a BM25 baseline built at\nidentical zero cost is significant at <i>p</i> = 5.7 &times; 10<sup>&minus;7</sup>; we did not test\nthat margin's reader sensitivity and flag it accordingly in Section XIV.</p>\"\"\"\nassert old_sum in s; s = s.replace(old_sum, new_sum)\n\nopen(\"paper-tkde.html\",\"w\").write(s)\nprint(\"abstract + findings updated:\", orig, \"->\", len(s))\nPY","description":"Correct abstract and findings for the reversal"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":216493,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":3977,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":216493,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3977,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":216493,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":216493},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":{"cache_miss_reason":{"type":"previous_message_not_found"}}},"requestId":"req_011Ce5YR2tJh1cGsSEBipZb5","type":"assistant","uuid":"3da0c779-96b0-408a-b373-010cbc2d7839","timestamp":"2026-08-16T01:16:09.193Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"fe41fb4b-5221-41ce-afce-6a9fa3dade0c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/graph-bench-results","sessionId":"27642e0f-a981-4143-aea0-6f4f8cb34d37","version":"2.1.226","gitBranch":"main","slug":"structured-meandering-origami"}
