{"parentUuid":"f7123999-f257-42fb-98f4-069875ddbd3e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce5YXL36S2mKXnnMx66Sq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now Section XII rebuilt around the full factorial — this is the paper's most important section now."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2889,"cache_read_input_tokens":220493,"output_tokens":2998,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2889,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2998,"cache_read_input_tokens":220493,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2889,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2889},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce5YXJQNR1Zkm36QAJyTh","type":"assistant","uuid":"9c12aeb5-ce3f-4d98-95ff-2cda9e671098","timestamp":"2026-08-16T01:16:57.933Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"fe41fb4b-5221-41ce-afce-6a9fa3dade0c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/graph-bench-results","sessionId":"27642e0f-a981-4143-aea0-6f4f8cb34d37","version":"2.1.226","gitBranch":"main","slug":"structured-meandering-origami"}
{"parentUuid":"9c12aeb5-ce3f-4d98-95ff-2cda9e671098","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce5YXL36S2mKXnnMx66Sq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CTJyhjCaD6TUbYH16FFSH9","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/graph-bench-results\npython3 - <<'PY'\ns=open(\"paper-tkde.html\").read()\ni=s.find('<h2>XII. Robustness Analysis</h2>')\nj=s.find('<h2>XIII. Threats to Validity</h2>')\nassert i>0 and j>i\nNEW = \"\"\"<h2>XII. Robustness Analysis</h2>\n\n<p class=\"first\">A single reader and judge is the principal threat to any result of this shape, and\nLLM-as-judge protocols carry known systematic biases [43]. We therefore ran the full reader &times;\njudge factorial, holding the banked retrievals fixed so that only the consuming models vary. Two\nmodel families are involved: an OpenAI-family reader and judge (the primary configuration) and an\nAnthropic-family reader and judge, plus a second OpenAI-family reader of a different model. Every\ncell is the same 1,540 paired questions with zero empty answers and zero judge failures.</p>\n\n<div class=\"tbl\">\n<table>\n  <caption>Table VI. <span class=\"cn\">LoCoMo margin across the reader &times; judge factorial</span></caption>\n  <thead><tr><th>Configuration</th><th>reader / judge</th><th class=\"n\">eg</th><th class=\"n\">mem0</th><th class=\"n\">&Delta;</th><th class=\"n\">b/c</th><th class=\"n\">p</th></tr></thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr><td>Primary (banked)</td><td>A / A</td><td class=\"n\">94.74</td><td class=\"n\">93.83</td><td class=\"n\">+0.91</td><td class=\"n\">43/29</td><td class=\"n\">0.125</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Control re-judge</td><td>A / A</td><td class=\"n\">94.48</td><td class=\"n\">94.03</td><td class=\"n\">+0.45</td><td class=\"n\">40/33</td><td class=\"n\">0.483</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Judge swap</td><td>A / B</td><td class=\"n\">94.48</td><td class=\"n\">93.51</td><td class=\"n\">+0.97</td><td class=\"n\">46/31</td><td class=\"n\">0.110</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Second reader</td><td>C / A</td><td class=\"n\">93.77</td><td class=\"n\">93.44</td><td class=\"n\">+0.32</td><td class=\"n\">52/47</td><td class=\"n\">0.688</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><b>Reader swap</b></td><td>B / A</td><td class=\"n\">96.56</td><td class=\"n\">96.69</td><td class=\"n\"><b>&minus;0.13</b></td><td class=\"n\">27/29</td><td class=\"n\">0.894</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Fully independent</td><td>B / B</td><td class=\"n\">96.88</td><td class=\"n\">96.62</td><td class=\"n\">+0.26</td><td class=\"n\">32/28</td><td class=\"n\">0.699</td></tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n\n<p class=\"nofirst\">Three findings follow, and we regard the third as the most important result in this\npaper's evaluation.</p>\n\n<p><i>The self-grading confound is refuted.</i> The obvious objection to an author-run evaluation is\nthat the judge favours the authors' system. Swapping the judge to a different model family\n<i>reproduces</i> the margin, +0.91 against +0.97, and an independent re-judge of the banked\nretrievals agrees with the harness labels on 99.6 percent of questions. Whatever is happening here,\nit is not the judge.</p>\n\n<p><i>The ordering reverses under a different reader.</i> Holding retrievals and judge fixed and\nchanging only the reader moves the margin from +0.91 to <b>&minus;0.13</b>: the competitor is ahead.\nNo cell in the table is significant, the primary configuration least of all, so the correct\ndescription is not that the result flipped but that <i>there was never an established effect to\nflip</i>. A margin whose confidence interval contains zero will change sign under perturbation, and\nthis one does. We report it because a reviewer who runs one different reader finds it immediately,\nand because the field's convention of reporting a single reader would have let us publish a\nfirst-place finish that the evidence does not support.</p>\n\n<p><i>The mechanism is reader headroom, not retrieval.</i> The stronger reader lifts <i>both</i>\nsystems, and lifts the competitor more: +2.86 against our +1.82. Both retrieval contexts already\ncontained the evidence; the weaker reader was the binding constraint, and relieving it compresses the\ndifference between the systems toward zero. This is consistent with Section XI-C, where\n<span class=\"mono\">P(correct | gold retrieved)</span> is 0.96 to 0.97 for every system. The\nimplication is general and uncomfortable for this literature: benchmark separations obtained with a\ngiven reader shrink as readers improve, so a memory-system ranking is a statement about a\nreader-benchmark pair and not a durable property of the systems.</p>\n\n<p>We therefore make no claim of superiority over inference-built memory on accuracy. The claims that\nsurvive the factorial are that entire-graph is never significantly behind on either benchmark, and\nthat it reaches that position at zero index cost, which is a count and not an estimate.</p>\n\n\"\"\"\ns = s[:i] + NEW + s[j:]\nopen(\"paper-tkde.html\",\"w\").write(s)\nprint(\"Section XII replaced\")\nPY\ngrep -n \"Table VI\\|Table V\\.\" paper-tkde.html | head","description":"Replace robustness section with factorial"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2889,"cache_read_input_tokens":220493,"output_tokens":2998,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2889,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2998,"cache_read_input_tokens":220493,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2889,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2889},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce5YXJQNR1Zkm36QAJyTh","type":"assistant","uuid":"0623182f-d145-42a0-a724-b4728a865b91","timestamp":"2026-08-16T01:17:19.198Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"fe41fb4b-5221-41ce-afce-6a9fa3dade0c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/graph-bench-results","sessionId":"27642e0f-a981-4143-aea0-6f4f8cb34d37","version":"2.1.226","gitBranch":"main","slug":"structured-meandering-origami"}
{"parentUuid":"0623182f-d145-42a0-a724-b4728a865b91","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"22aece5c-9924-4e9e-8a41-3e39834f4322","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CTJyhjCaD6TUbYH16FFSH9","type":"tool_result","content":"Section XII replaced\n818:  <caption>Table V. <span class=\"cn\">Index cost in currency, by price point (USD / Mtok in&thinsp;/&thinsp;out)</span></caption>\n886:  <caption>Table VI. <span class=\"cn\">LoCoMo margin across the reader &times; judge factorial</span></caption>","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"79b4d2f0-9e5a-4422-a8c5-ee4f607e508a","timestamp":"2026-08-16T01:17:19.314Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"Section XII replaced\n818:  <caption>Table V. <span class=\"cn\">Index cost in currency, by price point (USD / Mtok in&thinsp;/&thinsp;out)</span></caption>\n886:  <caption>Table VI. <span class=\"cn\">LoCoMo margin across the reader &times; judge factorial</span></caption>","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0623182f-d145-42a0-a724-b4728a865b91","session_id":"fe41fb4b-5221-41ce-afce-6a9fa3dade0c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/graph-bench-results","sessionId":"27642e0f-a981-4143-aea0-6f4f8cb34d37","version":"2.1.226","gitBranch":"main","slug":"structured-meandering-origami"}
{"parentUuid":"79b4d2f0-9e5a-4422-a8c5-ee4f607e508a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce5Ya3EPhrEoVwk8AXUE9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3116,"cache_read_input_tokens":223382,"output_tokens":2464,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3116,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2464,"cache_read_input_tokens":223382,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3116,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3116},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce5Ya1TUrasFJSdN4gCAV","type":"assistant","uuid":"defbed16-459c-403d-985a-9e7d9e34fc5a","timestamp":"2026-08-16T01:17:27.566Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"fe41fb4b-5221-41ce-afce-6a9fa3dade0c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/graph-bench-results","sessionId":"27642e0f-a981-4143-aea0-6f4f8cb34d37","version":"2.1.226","gitBranch":"main","slug":"structured-meandering-origami"}
{"parentUuid":"defbed16-459c-403d-985a-9e7d9e34fc5a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce5Ya3EPhrEoVwk8AXUE9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SGSZCF6obKuZTNxVfuLG9e","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/graph-bench-results\npython3 - <<'PY'\ns=open(\"paper-tkde.html\").read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert a in s, \"MISS: \"+a[:70]\n    s=s.replace(a,b)\n\n# XI-A accuracy narrative\nrep(\"\"\"McNemar <i>p</i> = 0.125, and the bootstrap interval [&minus;0.19, +2.01]\nincludes zero. Section XII shows this margin narrowing further under a reader swap. The defensible\nclaim is parity, and it is the one we make.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"McNemar <i>p</i> = 0.125, and the bootstrap interval [&minus;0.19, +2.01]\nincludes zero. Section XII shows this margin <i>reversing</i> to &minus;0.13 when only the reader\nmodel is changed. The defensible claim is parity, and it is the one we make. Table I is the primary\npre-registered configuration and should be read together with Table VI, not on its own.\"\"\")\n\n# XIII external validity — two benchmarks now\nrep(\"\"\"<p><i>External validity.</i> One benchmark, one corpus genre, one reader family in the primary\nconfiguration. LongMemEval [39] and other long-context memory benchmarks are not covered here.\nGenerality across benchmarks is explicitly <i>not</i> established, and the cost result&mdash;which is\narchitectural rather than empirical&mdash;is the only finding we expect to transfer unchanged.</p>\"\"\",\n\"\"\"<p><i>External validity.</i> Two benchmarks of one genre&mdash;long multi-session\nconversation&mdash;and two reader families. The direction of the accuracy result agrees across both\nbenchmarks and the magnitude reaches significance on neither. Section XII shows the LoCoMo ordering is\nreader-dependent; we did not run the equivalent factorial on LongMemEval, so its +2.20 should be\nassumed to carry the same sensitivity until tested. Code corpora, on which this index was originally\nbuilt, are not evaluated here at all. The cost result&mdash;architectural rather than\nempirical&mdash;is the only finding we expect to transfer unchanged.</p>\"\"\")\n\n# XIV limitations — evaluation scope\nrep(\"\"\"<p><i>Evaluation scope.</i> One benchmark, and a margin over the strongest competitor that does not\nclear significance under any reader tested. Section XII states this rather than burying it.</p>\"\"\",\n\"\"\"<p><i>Evaluation scope.</i> Two benchmarks, and a margin over the strongest competitor that clears\nsignificance under no reader tested and changes sign under one. Section XII states this rather than\nburying it. One consequence deserves emphasis: our ablations and the BM25 comparison were measured\nunder the primary reader only. The 2.86-point BM25 margin is the paper's one significant accuracy\nresult, and we have not established that it is reader-independent; by the mechanism of Section XII it\nwould be expected to compress under a stronger reader, though it starts from four times the noise\nfloor rather than from within it.</p>\"\"\")\n\n# XV conclusion\nrep(\"\"\"We close on the narrow claim rather than the broad one. We do not argue that structural retrieval\nis more accurate than inference-built retrieval: our margin is 0.91 points, it does not clear\nsignificance, and it narrows to 0.32 under a reader swap. We argue something we can defend exactly.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"We close on the narrow claim rather than the broad one. We do not argue that structural retrieval\nis more accurate than inference-built retrieval. Our margin is 0.91 points on one benchmark and 2.20\non another, it clears significance on neither, and under one reader it changes sign. We argue\nsomething we can defend exactly.\"\"\")\n\nrep(\"\"\"Applied to conversation with a single mapping decision and no preprocessing, it ranks first of eight\nsystems on a conversational-memory benchmark, recovering all gold evidence by rank 10 on 82.0\npercent of questions against 56.8 percent for the next measurable system, while consuming zero tokens\nto build its index against a measured 50.85 million for the strongest competitor.</p>\"\"\",\n\"\"\"Applied to conversation with a single mapping decision and no preprocessing, it ranks first of eight\nsystems on one conversational-memory benchmark and leads on a second, recovering all gold evidence by\nrank 10 on 82.0 percent of questions against 56.8 percent for the next measurable system, while\nconsuming zero tokens to build its index against a measured 50.85 million for the strongest\ncompetitor. Neither accuracy margin is significant, and Section XII shows one of them is\nreader-dependent.</p>\"\"\")\n\nopen(\"paper-tkde.html\",\"w\").write(s)\nprint(\"narrative reconciled\")\nPY\n\"/Applications/Google Chrome.app/Contents/MacOS/Google Chrome\" --headless --disable-gpu --no-pdf-header-footer --print-to-pdf=entire-graph-tkde.pdf \"file:///Users/suhaan/devenv/graph-bench-results/paper-tkde.html\" 2>&1 | grep -v task_policy | tail -1\nsleep 5\npython3 -c \"\nimport re,html\nd=open('entire-graph-tkde.pdf','rb').read()\ns=open('paper-tkde.html').read()\nt=html.unescape(re.sub(r'<[^>]+>',' ',re.sub(r'<(script|style).*?</\\1>','',s,flags=re.S)))\nprint('pages:',len(re.findall(rb'/Type\\s*/Page[^s]',d)),'| words:',len(t.split()),'| refs:',s.count('<li>')-6)\"","description":"Reconcile narrative and rebuild","timeout":300000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3116,"cache_read_input_tokens":223382,"output_tokens":2464,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3116,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2464,"cache_read_input_tokens":223382,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3116,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3116},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce5Ya1TUrasFJSdN4gCAV","type":"assistant","uuid":"9b5f5744-f262-43c3-925f-19ed751aebd7","timestamp":"2026-08-16T01:17:48.542Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"fe41fb4b-5221-41ce-afce-6a9fa3dade0c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/graph-bench-results","sessionId":"27642e0f-a981-4143-aea0-6f4f8cb34d37","version":"2.1.226","gitBranch":"main","slug":"structured-meandering-origami"}
