{"parentUuid":"fce1b948-8a84-4cca-a693-327b08e53eca","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"22aece5c-9924-4e9e-8a41-3e39834f4322","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HCqJRDcKmeRYzJyfyBGE87","type":"tool_result","content":"681:McNemar <i>p</i> = 0.125, and the bootstrap interval [&minus;0.19, +2.01] includes zero. Section XII\n682-shows this margin narrowing further under a reader swap. The defensible claim is parity, and it is\n683-the one we make. Margins over the remaining systems, from 1.9 to 17.1 points, are well clear of the\n684-0.65-point noise floor.</p>\n738:<p class=\"nofirst\">The margin is 2.20 points with a discordant split of 40 to 29, bootstrap interval\n739-[&minus;1.00, +5.40] and <i>p</i> = 0.228. It is larger than the LoCoMo margin and, like it, does not\n740-reach significance. The direction is the same on both benchmarks and the magnitude is not\n741-distinguishable from zero on either.</p>","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"6f648343-1aab-425c-8fb1-785f65f83049","timestamp":"2026-08-16T01:18:01.326Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"681:McNemar <i>p</i> = 0.125, and the bootstrap interval [&minus;0.19, +2.01] includes zero. Section XII\n682-shows this margin narrowing further under a reader swap. The defensible claim is parity, and it is\n683-the one we make. Margins over the remaining systems, from 1.9 to 17.1 points, are well clear of the\n684-0.65-point noise floor.</p>\n738:<p class=\"nofirst\">The margin is 2.20 points with a discordant split of 40 to 29, bootstrap interval\n739-[&minus;1.00, +5.40] and <i>p</i> = 0.228. It is larger than the LoCoMo margin and, like it, does not\n740-reach significance. The direction is the same on both benchmarks and the magnitude is not\n741-distinguishable from zero on either.</p>","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"fce1b948-8a84-4cca-a693-327b08e53eca","session_id":"fe41fb4b-5221-41ce-afce-6a9fa3dade0c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/graph-bench-results","sessionId":"27642e0f-a981-4143-aea0-6f4f8cb34d37","version":"2.1.226","gitBranch":"main","slug":"structured-meandering-origami"}
{"parentUuid":"6f648343-1aab-425c-8fb1-785f65f83049","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce5YdC4YEm3iVgyprQbUw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BXgMCzi4yN2VFrZj7B5srn","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/graph-bench-results\npython3 - <<'PY'\ns=open(\"paper-tkde.html\").read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert a in s, \"MISS: \"+a[:60]\n    s=s.replace(a,b)\n\nrep(\"\"\"[&minus;0.19, +2.01] includes zero. Section XII\nshows this margin narrowing further under a reader swap. The defensible claim is parity, and it is\nthe one we make.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"[&minus;0.19, +2.01] includes zero. Section XII\nshows this margin <i>reversing</i> to &minus;0.13 when only the reader model is changed. The\ndefensible claim is parity, and it is the one we make. Table I is the primary pre-registered\nconfiguration and must be read together with Table VI, not on its own.\"\"\")\n\nrep(\"\"\"<p><i>External validity.</i> One benchmark, one corpus genre, one reader family in the primary\nconfiguration. LongMemEval [39] and other long-context memory benchmarks are not covered here.\nGenerality across benchmarks is explicitly <i>not</i> established, and the cost result&mdash;which is\narchitectural rather than empirical&mdash;is the only finding we expect to transfer unchanged.</p>\"\"\",\n\"\"\"<p><i>External validity.</i> Two benchmarks of one genre&mdash;long multi-session\nconversation&mdash;and two reader families. The direction of the accuracy result agrees across both\nbenchmarks and its magnitude reaches significance on neither. Section XII shows the LoCoMo ordering is\nreader-dependent; we did not run the equivalent factorial on LongMemEval, so its +2.20 should be\nassumed to carry the same sensitivity until tested. Code corpora, for which this index was originally\nbuilt, are not evaluated here at all. The cost result&mdash;architectural rather than\nempirical&mdash;is the only finding we expect to transfer unchanged.</p>\"\"\")\n\nrep(\"\"\"<p><i>Evaluation scope.</i> One benchmark, and a margin over the strongest competitor that does not\nclear significance under any reader tested. Section XII states this rather than burying it.</p>\"\"\",\n\"\"\"<p><i>Evaluation scope.</i> Two benchmarks, and a margin over the strongest competitor that clears\nsignificance under no reader tested and changes sign under one. One consequence deserves emphasis:\nour ablations and the BM25 comparison were measured under the primary reader only. The 2.86-point\nBM25 margin is the paper's one significant accuracy result, and we have not established that it is\nreader-independent; by the mechanism of Section XII it should be expected to compress under a\nstronger reader, though it starts from four times the noise floor rather than from within it.</p>\"\"\")\n\nrep(\"\"\"is more accurate than inference-built retrieval: our margin is 0.91 points, it does not clear\nsignificance, and it narrows to 0.32 under a reader swap. We argue something we can defend exactly.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"is more accurate than inference-built retrieval. Our margin is 0.91 points on one benchmark and 2.20\non another, it clears significance on neither, and under one reader it changes sign. We argue\nsomething we can defend exactly.\"\"\")\n\nrep(\"\"\"it ranks first of eight\nsystems on a conversational-memory benchmark, recovering all gold evidence by rank 10 on 82.0\npercent of questions against 56.8 percent for the next measurable system, while consuming zero tokens\nto build its index against a measured 50.85 million for the strongest competitor.</p>\"\"\",\n\"\"\"it ranks first of eight\nsystems on one conversational-memory benchmark and leads on a second, recovering all gold evidence by\nrank 10 on 82.0 percent of questions against 56.8 percent for the next measurable system, while\nconsuming zero tokens to build its index against a measured 50.85 million for the strongest\ncompetitor. Neither accuracy margin is significant, and Section XII shows one of them is\nreader-dependent.</p>\"\"\")\n\nopen(\"paper-tkde.html\",\"w\").write(s)\nprint(\"all 5 applied\")\nPY\n\"/Applications/Google Chrome.app/Contents/MacOS/Google Chrome\" --headless --disable-gpu --no-pdf-header-footer --print-to-pdf=entire-graph-tkde.pdf \"file:///Users/suhaan/devenv/graph-bench-results/paper-tkde.html\" 2>&1 | grep -v task_policy | tail -1\nsleep 5\npython3 -c \"\nimport re,html\nd=open('entire-graph-tkde.pdf','rb').read()\ns=open('paper-tkde.html').read()\nt=html.unescape(re.sub(r'<[^>]+>',' ',re.sub(r'<(script|style).*?</\\1>','',s,flags=re.S)))\nprint('pages:',len(re.findall(rb'/Type\\s*/Page[^s]',d)),'| words:',len(t.split()),'| refs:',s.count('<li>')-6)\"","description":"Apply narrative fixes and rebuild","timeout":300000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":453,"cache_read_input_tokens":229106,"output_tokens":1762,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":453,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1762,"cache_read_input_tokens":229106,"cache_creation_input_tokens":453,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":453},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce5Yd8B8WzcsUsaDTtjVS","type":"assistant","uuid":"a8afd26d-3960-4836-9725-11ed3933ec28","timestamp":"2026-08-16T01:18:20.284Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"fe41fb4b-5221-41ce-afce-6a9fa3dade0c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/graph-bench-results","sessionId":"27642e0f-a981-4143-aea0-6f4f8cb34d37","version":"2.1.226","gitBranch":"main","slug":"structured-meandering-origami"}
