{"parentUuid":"d0f25889-e2ee-438a-a443-6ed3e5a10059","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce5YiozAeZAMqXcxaRsXV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":213,"cache_read_input_tokens":237065,"output_tokens":1539,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":213,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1539,"cache_read_input_tokens":237065,"cache_creation_input_tokens":213,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":213},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce5YinJTgXQXmT4jaMwC7","type":"assistant","uuid":"2cbca760-517a-481f-9809-03fda6487016","timestamp":"2026-08-16T01:19:26.946Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"fe41fb4b-5221-41ce-afce-6a9fa3dade0c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/graph-bench-results","sessionId":"27642e0f-a981-4143-aea0-6f4f8cb34d37","version":"2.1.226","gitBranch":"main","slug":"structured-meandering-origami"}
{"parentUuid":"2cbca760-517a-481f-9809-03fda6487016","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce5YiozAeZAMqXcxaRsXV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**The result did not survive.** entire-graph does not reliably beat mem0 on accuracy, and the paper now says so.\n\n## The factorial\n\nHolding retrievals fixed and varying only the consuming models, across all 1,540 paired questions:\n\n| config | reader/judge | eg | mem0 | Δ | p |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| primary | A/A | 94.74 | 93.83 | +0.91 | 0.125 |\n| judge swap | A/B | 94.48 | 93.51 | +0.97 | 0.110 |\n| second reader | C/A | 93.77 | 93.44 | +0.32 | 0.688 |\n| **reader swap** | **B/A** | **96.56** | **96.69** | **−0.13** | 0.894 |\n| fully independent | B/B | 96.88 | 96.62 | +0.26 | 0.699 |\n\nUnder one reader, **mem0 is ahead**. Nothing anywhere reaches significance.\n\nThree things came out of this, and the third is the most interesting finding in the evaluation:\n\n**The self-grading objection is dead.** Swapping the judge to a different model family *reproduces* the margin (+0.91 → +0.97), and an independent re-judge agrees with the harness on 99.6%. That was the most likely attack on an author-run comparison and it doesn't land.\n\n**The reversal isn't a flip, it's a collapse.** The primary result was never significant — CI [−0.19, +2.01]. A margin containing zero changes sign under perturbation. There was no established effect to overturn.\n\n**The mechanism is reader headroom.** The stronger reader lifts *both* systems and lifts mem0 more (+2.86 vs our +1.82). Both contexts already held the evidence; the weaker reader was the constraint. That generalizes uncomfortably for this whole literature — memory-system rankings are statements about a reader-benchmark pair, not durable properties, and they shrink as readers improve.\n\n## LongMemEval closed, and it holds\n\nProvenance established (`eg_matrix.sh`, plain eg, 0/500 profiles vs 498/500 for the v2 build). Same-window, both arms concurrent: **eg 89.60 vs mem0 87.40, +2.20, p=0.228**. The cross-window version gave an identical +2.20 — the drift I was worried about wasn't moving this comparison at all.\n\n## What the paper claims now\n\nParity on accuracy across two benchmarks — never significantly ahead, never significantly behind — at **zero index tokens against 50.85M**. The factorial is now a stated contribution rather than a buried caveat, on the grounds that single-reader protocols are the norm and cannot detect this.\n\nThat's a defensible TKDE paper. The version claiming a first-place finish would have died on the first reviewer who swapped a reader.\n\n**One thing this surfaced that I'd previously called safe:** the BM25 margin (+2.86, p=5.7e-07) is the paper's only significant accuracy result, and it was measured under the primary reader only. By the mechanism above it should compress under a stronger reader. It starts from four times the noise floor rather than inside it, so it likely survives — but it's untested, and I've flagged it in Limitations rather than assumed it.\n\n**Still blocking submission:** author names, affiliation, licence; the BM25 granularity control; and the BM25 reader-sensitivity check that this factorial just made necessary."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":213,"cache_read_input_tokens":237065,"output_tokens":1539,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":213,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1539,"cache_read_input_tokens":237065,"cache_creation_input_tokens":213,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":213},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce5YinJTgXQXmT4jaMwC7","type":"assistant","uuid":"1d60b9f3-a57d-4657-b6b8-79a330f9b632","timestamp":"2026-08-16T01:19:41.760Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"fe41fb4b-5221-41ce-afce-6a9fa3dade0c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/graph-bench-results","sessionId":"27642e0f-a981-4143-aea0-6f4f8cb34d37","version":"2.1.226","gitBranch":"main","slug":"structured-meandering-origami"}
