{"parentUuid":"ada83283-164f-4f67-958c-d784cc20346c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce7LFaMEAttJDP5vbUDBi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2161,"cache_read_input_tokens":238877,"output_tokens":1394,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2161,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1394,"cache_read_input_tokens":238877,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2161,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2161},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce7LFEHEURTdUoRtXvxyn","type":"assistant","uuid":"d52d8c3d-1a8a-4168-a528-000037c07f8f","timestamp":"2026-08-16T23:57:10.132Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"fe41fb4b-5221-41ce-afce-6a9fa3dade0c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/graph-bench-results","sessionId":"27642e0f-a981-4143-aea0-6f4f8cb34d37","version":"2.1.226","gitBranch":"main","slug":"structured-meandering-origami"}
{"parentUuid":"d52d8c3d-1a8a-4168-a528-000037c07f8f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce7LFaMEAttJDP5vbUDBi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`gcloud` auth expired mid-session, so the VM is unreachable until you re-auth: type **`! gcloud auth login`**.\n\n## Progress on the goal\n\n**The manuscript is essentially there.** 12pp, 9,436 words, 43 refs, 7 figures, 6 tables — structurally a TKDE paper rather than a conference paper stretched:\n\n- Formal problem formulation with the cost model; complexity analysis\n- Related work as a six-part taxonomy (was 21 refs, now 43)\n- Experimental setup split from results; reproducibility section\n- **Two** benchmarks — LME came in at +2.20 same-window with provenance established\n- Robustness factorial; threats to validity across all four types\n\n**What's left:** the BM25 controls (needs the VM), author names/affiliation/licence (needs you), PR #104 merged + a DOI.\n\n## Meanwhile — the gap a reviewer will actually hit\n\nThe paper describes a *code* index and evaluates it entirely on *prose*. Section V claims determinism, incremental construction, and seconds-scale builds, and right now those claims carry no measurements. That's fixable locally with no API cost, so I'm doing it while the VM is down."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2161,"cache_read_input_tokens":238877,"output_tokens":1394,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2161,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1394,"cache_read_input_tokens":238877,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2161,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2161},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"re