{"type":"bridge-session","sessionId":"27642e0f-a981-4143-aea0-6f4f8cb34d37","bridgeSessionId":"cse_015igKU9YpcFoeCFDccAcvXX","lastSequenceNum":16531}
{"parentUuid":"7b38a1a6-78f6-4362-bc8c-d8d01cd2a489","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce7LZewZ7m9t9SPtaR7Dp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015rEMyhgL2cPEEonr3htQo6","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/graph-bench-results\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport re\ns=open(\"paper-tkde.html\").read()\n\n# shift existing Table I..VI -> II..VII (high to low, sentinel to avoid collisions)\nfor old,new in [(\"VI\",\"@7@\"),(\"V\",\"@6@\"),(\"IV\",\"@5@\"),(\"III\",\"@4@\"),(\"II\",\"@3@\"),(\"I\",\"@2@\")]:\n    s=re.sub(r\"Table %s\\b\"%old, \"Table %s\"%new, s)\nfor tok,rom in [(\"@7@\",\"VII\"),(\"@6@\",\"VI\"),(\"@5@\",\"V\"),(\"@4@\",\"IV\"),(\"@3@\",\"III\"),(\"@2@\",\"II\")]:\n    s=s.replace(\"Table \"+tok, \"Table \"+rom)\n\nNEW = \"\"\"<h3>C. Measured construction cost and determinism</h3>\n\n<p class=\"first\">Because the system's central claims are about construction rather than accuracy, we\nmeasure construction directly on four production repositories spanning 164 to 462 thousand lines and\ntwo language families. Each was indexed twice, independently, and the full serialised graph was\nhashed both times.</p>\n\n<div class=\"tbl\">\n<table>\n  <caption>Table I. <span class=\"cn\">Index construction on production repositories</span></caption>\n  <thead><tr><th>Repository</th><th class=\"n\">kLOC</th><th class=\"n\">Files</th><th class=\"n\">Symbols</th><th class=\"n\">Relations</th><th class=\"n\">Build (s)</th><th class=\"n\">kLOC/s</th></tr></thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr><td>entire-api (Go)</td><td class=\"n\">163.9</td><td class=\"n\">727</td><td class=\"n\">12,806</td><td class=\"n\">57,363</td><td class=\"n\">11.72</td><td class=\"n\">14.0</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>entire.io (TS)</td><td class=\"n\">399.3</td><td class=\"n\">1,708</td><td class=\"n\">29,402</td><td class=\"n\">90,026</td><td class=\"n\">33.16</td><td class=\"n\">12.0</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>cli (Go)</td><td class=\"n\">411.7</td><td class=\"n\">1,199</td><td class=\"n\">23,767</td><td class=\"n\">130,073</td><td class=\"n\">25.01</td><td class=\"n\">16.5</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>entiredb (Go)</td><td class=\"n\">462.3</td><td class=\"n\">2,543</td><td class=\"n\">36,068</td><td class=\"n\">198,924</td><td class=\"n\">33.91</td><td class=\"n\">13.6</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><b>Total</b></td><td class=\"n\"><b>1,437</b></td><td class=\"n\"><b>6,177</b></td><td class=\"n\"><b>102,043</b></td><td class=\"n\"><b>476,386</b></td><td class=\"n\"><b>103.8</b></td><td class=\"n\"><b>13.8</b></td></tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n\n<p class=\"nofirst\">Two results follow. <i>Determinism holds empirically.</i> The two independent\nbuilds produced <b>byte-identical</b> serialised graphs on all four repositories, verified by SHA-256\nover the complete record stream, not by spot-checking summary counts. This is the property asserted\nin Section V-D and it is what licenses the maintenance term of Section II being zero.</p>\n\n<p><i>Throughput is near-constant in corpus size.</i> Across a 2.8&times; range in lines and a\n3.5&times; range in relations, throughput varies only between 12.0 and 16.5 kLOC/s, with no downward\ntrend as repositories grow. That is the behaviour the complexity analysis predicts&mdash;linear\nparsing plus a logarithmic resolution factor, with no global fixpoint&mdash;and it is what makes\nrebuilding an entire 1.4-million-line corpus a 104-second operation rather than a scheduled job.\nIndexing all four repositories from scratch costs less wall-clock than a single one of the 5,882\nextraction calls the strongest competitor makes per corpus, and costs zero tokens.</p>\n\n<p>These figures are single-run on one machine and are reported to establish order of magnitude and\nthe determinism property, not to support a throughput comparison against another indexer.</p>\n\n<h2>VIII. Code and Prose in One Index</h2>\"\"\"\ns=s.replace(\"<h2>VIII. Code and Prose in One Index</h2>\", NEW, 1)\nopen(\"paper-tkde.html\",\"w\").write(s)\nprint(\"Table I inserted; all tables renumbered\")\nPY\ngrep -o \"Table [IVX]\\+\\.\" paper-tkde.html | sort | uniq -c\n\"/Applications/Google Chrome.app/Contents/MacOS/Google Chrome\" --headless --disable-gpu --no-pdf-header-footer --print-to-pdf=entire-graph-tkde.pdf \"file:///Users/suhaan/devenv/graph-bench-results/paper-tkde.html\" 2>&1 | grep -v task_policy | tail -1\nsleep 5\npython3 -c \"\nimport re,html\nd=open('entire-graph-tkde.pdf','rb').read(); s=open('paper-tkde.html').read()\nt=html.unescape(re.sub(r'<[^>]+>',' ',re.sub(r'<(script|style).*?</\\1>','',s,flags=re.S)))\nprint('pages:',len(re.findall(rb'/Type\\s*/Page[^s]',d)),'| words:',len(t.split()))\"","description":"Insert measured-construction table and renumber","timeout":300000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2395,"cache_read_input_tokens":251000,"output_tokens":1978,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2395,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1978,"cache_read_input_tokens":251000,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2395,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2395},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce7LZXiEKhHgKCN9XwdDm","type":"assistant","uuid":"b9922a69-0e81-42dc-8a6e-704cb2463c0f","timestamp":"2026-08-17T00:01:29.548Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"fe41fb4b-5221-41ce-afce-6a9fa3dade0c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/graph-bench-results","sessionId":"27642e0f-a981-4143-aea0-6f4f8cb34d37","version":"2.1.226","gitBranch":"main","slug":"structured-meandering-origami"}
