{"parentUuid":"8669bfb9-9749-4f24-ab42-3602709f6fb6","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"60a284a6-cb88-4cdf-b4ce-715939dca4f6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01N334g3KMrvviJHtsUA6KFx","type":"tool_result","content":"Suhaan Thayyil\nthayyilsuhaan@gmail.com | (803) 558-1636 | github.com/suhaanthayyil\nE D U C AT I O N\n63817542053\nMarvin Ridge High School\tSep 2025 – May 2029\nWaxhaw, NC · Focus: Computer Science · Class Rank: 2 / 460 · GPA: 4.682 W, 4.0 UW Coursework: AP Computer Science A, AP Computer Science Principles\nSouth Piedmont Community College\tJan 2026 – May 2029\nDual Enrollment, Online\nIntroduction to Mechatronics CTE Certificate (C40350PB): CIS 110 Introduction to Computers\nBusiness Administration CTE Certificate (C25120PA): BUS 137 Principles of Management, ACC 120 Principles of Financial Accounting\n638175260788R E S E A R C H\nPathway-based machine learning is competitive with but does not exceed PAM50-ROR for breast cancer prognosis\nA pre-registered multi-cohort benchmark in 4,532 patients\nJan 2026 – Apr 2026\nFirst Author · Preprint: doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20518165 · 150+ Downloads · Round 2 of peer review at BMC Artificial Intelligence\nTrained a survival prediction model on TCGA gene expression data and tested it on two outside datasets, SCAN-B and GSE96058, to evaluate generalization to new patients.\nUsed pathway-level features, Cox regression, binary classification, and SHAP values to identify which biological pathways most influence patient outcomes.\nAppraised by Dr. Eliezer Van Allen of the Dana-Farber Cancer Institute / Harvard Medical School.\nPredicting Severe COVID-19 Requiring Hospitalization with Machine Learning\tDec 2025 – Apr 2026\nA comparison of four classiﬁers and SHAP explainability on a large population dataset\nFirst Author · Published in NHSJS (National High School Journal of Science) · Paper\nAnalyzed clinical predictors and demographic patterns in Long COVID patients using machine learning to identify the factors most associated with persistent symptoms.\nE X P E R I E N C E\n63817542275\nSoftware Engineering Intern — Entire\tJun 2026 – Present\nBuilt an automated code-evaluation tool that ranks GitHub repositories on a composite quality score using multiple analysis lenses, each producing a verdict backed by reasoning and evidence drawn from session transcripts, distilled facts, and git history; deployed it across 10 team submissions.\nDesigned and shipped interactive terminal dashboards (TUIs) for the evaluation tool and the platform’s knowledge store, surfacing per-repository scoring, summaries, findings, and semantic search directly in the terminal.\nIntegrated the platform’s semantic-diff layer into the evaluation pipeline to compare what teams built versus what they planned; delivered all work through reviewed pull requests with test coverage and bug fixes.\nResearch Assistant — Caltech\tJun 2026 – Present\nRemote / Pasadena, CA\nAssist Kevin S. Fleisher, a Caltech Applied Physics graduate student, under Dr. Thompson on computational research.\nHelp develop machine learning models to predict cell fate transitions during differentiation.\nAssist with analysis of single-cell gene expression data to understand how cells move between biological states, identify factors that influence differentiation outcomes, and study the regulatory patterns that drive cells toward specific fates.\nResearcher — UC San Diego School of Medicine\tMay 2026 – Present Carter Lab · Remote / San Diego, CA\nDeveloping a summer research project with Dr. Hannah Carter’s lab focused on computational cancer variant interpretation and protein-interface variant modeling.\nPreparing datasets, benchmarks, and analysis plans for machine-learning evaluation of biological variant effects.\nLead Programmer — VEX Robotics Team 16885B\tOct 2025 – Mar 2026 Waxhaw, NC\nLed all programming for the competition robot, including autonomous driving, sensor reading, and real-time decision making.\nBuilt navigation and control systems and wrote telemetry tools to track robot performance during matches.\nAcademic Tutor — NextGen Tutoring\tJan 2024 – Aug 2025\nRemote · nextgentutoring.pythonanywhere.com\nTutored 10 students in math and computer science.\nLibrary Volunteer — Fort Mill Public Library\tJun–Jul 2024 & Jun–Jul 2025 Fort Mill, SC\nSupported community programs and daily library operations.\nS E L E C T E D P R O J E C T S\n63817542260\nRelay — Real-Time Accessibility Middleware\tApr 2026\nElectron, Node.js, Deepgram Nova-3, GPT-4o, MediaPipe, YAMNet · relay-six-topaz.vercel.app\nCross-platform desktop and mobile overlay translating speech, sound, screen, and gesture into accessible output for deaf and blind users; 6 real-time subsystems, sub-second caption latency. 2nd Place NC State, TSA Software Development 2026.\nCurriculon — AI Education Tool\tJan 2026\nNext.js, FastAPI, CrewAI, ChromaDB, Redis, SQL · curriculonai.com\nMulti-agent AI system generating complete curricula (units, lessons, assessments) for AP / IB / college / HS levels; 96.4% alignment accuracy.\nEvidence Finder — AI Research Tool\tDec 2025\nNext.js, FastAPI, LangChain, ChromaDB · evidence-finder-alpha.vercel.app\nAI tool that searches the web, pulls relevant evidence, and organizes it for debate and research use.\nRecipeSmith — iOS App (Published on App Store)\tNov 2025 Swift, OpenAI API · App Store\nBuilt and published an AI recipe app with nutritional analysis, AI-generated food images, and step-by-step cooking instructions.\nMulti-Disease CT Scan Detector\tDec 2022\nTensorFlow · 80% Accuracy · github.com/suhaanthayyil/Covid19\nTrained a CNN to detect tuberculosis, COVID-19, and pneumonia from CT scans simultaneously with 80% accuracy.\nReinforcement Learning Mario AI\tMar 2022\nPython, PyTorch · github.com/suhaanthayyil/RLMario\nBuilt a deep Q-learning agent that teaches itself to play Super Mario Bros through trial and error.\nT E C H N I C A L S K I L L S\n63817542454\nLanguages: Python (6+ yrs), Java (1+ yrs), Swift (2+ yrs), JavaScript / TypeScript (1+ yrs), HTML / CSS (3+ yrs)\nML / AI: PyTorch, TensorFlow, Hugging Face, scikit-learn, LangChain, LangGraph, AutoGen, CrewAI, RAG, fine-tuning, prompt engineering\nWeb Frameworks: Next.js, React, FastAPI, Flask, Django, Streamlit\nCloud & Deployment: AWS (Certified), Google Cloud, Vercel, Railway, Docker, GitHub Actions, serverless architecture\nDatabases & Tools: ChromaDB, PostgreSQL, Redis, Firebase, Git, Weights & Biases\nSpecialized: Computer Vision, CNNs, NLP, Reinforcement Learning, Web Scraping, API Integration, Bioinformatics (Cox regression, SHAP, TCGA pipelines)\nA C T I V I T I E S & L E A D E R S H I P\n63817542202\nDirector of Coding / Programming Events, Marvin Ridge TSA (May 2026 – Present)\nInnovation Hub Co-Manager, Marvin Ridge Computer Science Club (May 2026 – Present)\nNSDA Speech & Debate — Active member, Lincoln-Douglas and Public Forum divisions (Sep 2025 – Present)\nC E R T I F I C AT I O N S & AWA R D S\n63817542338\nAWS Certified AI Practitioner — Feb 2025 – Feb 2028 (Credential: 8757c9af62694d8c9a433c0dbccc20f3)\nNSDA — 2nd Place Rising Stars PF, Capstone Tournament, Dec 2025 (5–0 prelim record, 29 avg speaker points)\nTSA — 2nd Place, NC State, Software Development (2026)\nFBLA — Top 10, NC State, Website Coding & Development (2026)\nBETA Club — 3rd Place, SC State, Computer Science Principles (2025)\nRobotics — Create Award, State Qualifying Local Competition (2026)\nA D D I T I O N A L I N F O R M AT I O N\n63817542311\nLanguages: English (Native), Hindi (Native), Spanish (Working Proficiency)\nInterests: AI / ML research, app development, robotics, tennis, trading & technical analysis\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/suhaan/devenv","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"d9d5ddf6-a607-45db-a7a8-d3807e7a4094","timestamp":"2026-08-17T00:33:05.370Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"Suhaan Thayyil\nthayyilsuhaan@gmail.com | (803) 558-1636 | github.com/suhaanthayyil\nE D U