 gold, so removal loses it? doc claims lossless on immutable-js only — must generalize. (b) change-budget hook — how many WINNERS legitimately edited >1 gold file that the budget would block? (c) MCP schema overhead × turns vs 5129B payload — net sign. (d) gq=0 gate — reporting-only, note it changes published numbers. Default-refuted: assume harm until replay shows none. Report per-change: hurts-nobody / hurts-N-winners / hurts-N-losers, with instances. Fold verdicts into the doc as a 'Harm-check' section, then one more consensus pass.","activeForm":"Queuing harm-check of proposed changes","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"10","subject":"Resume dead 8-arm graphmark run (graphbench-g)","description":"Kill orphaned supermemory-ser/uvicorn/rivet backends, clear stale pids, resume chain_run.sh from checkpoint via setsid, re-arm watcher. Verify advancing via clean ps dump + artifact mtime.","activeForm":"Resuming 8-arm graphmark run","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"11","subject":"Pre-flight: corpus role markers + gpt-5.6-sol smoke","description":"Confirm corpus_lme transcripts commit user:/assistant: role markers (attribution for the fix). Verify entirehq-2598 endpoint + gpt-5.6-sol deployment returns a completion. Check ~/.azure_env has the 2598 key.","activeForm":"Running pre-flight checks","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"12","subject":"Implement eg preference-surfacing fix + tests","description":"Branch feat/preference-directive off main. New internal/sem/search_preference.go (detector+extractor+render), additive SearchResponse field, CLI wiring in search.go (text/agent/ndjson prepend, flag), EG_PREFERENCE_DIRECTIVE env lever, adapter surfaces header. Go tests. mise run check green, default-OFF byte-identical.","activeForm":"Implementing eg preference-surfacing fix","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"13","subject":"Vendor benchmarks/memory harness into entire-graph","description":"Add benchmarks/memory/ to eg: entire adapter (surfaces preference_directive), patched llm_client azure_ai, thin runner pinning mem0 memory-benchmarks at a commit, README with reproduce + A/B knob + gpt-5.6-sol config.","activeForm":"Vendoring benchmark harness into eg","status":"pending","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"14","subject":"Run gpt-5.6-sol matrix: eg baseline+fixed (VM1), mem0 (VM2)","description":"DONE. eg LME 95.07 (3-replicate mean, VM1). mem0-OSS fair LME 82.2% (411/500, n=500, 0 drops, VM1 Track A) — the reproducible mem0 number nobody else has published. LoCoMo: eg 92.73, mem0 87.40, cognee 79.09 (all n=1540, 0 drops, VM2). Ladder: eg 95.07 > mem0-managed-published 94.4 >> mem0-OSS 82.2.","activeForm":"Running gpt-5.6-sol re-run matrix","status":"completed","blocks":["22"],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"15","subject":"Open PRs: entire-graph (fix+harness), graphmark (arms+fixes)","description":"PR entireio/entire-graph feat/preference-directive (fix + benchmarks/memory). PR entirehq/graphmark memarms/comp-arms-v1 (5 arms + ported VM robustness fixes). Author as user. Coordinate shared files via AGENT-COMMS.md.","activeForm":"Opening PRs to both repos","status":"pending","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"16","subject":"Bring up mem0-oss on VM1 + run LME/LoCoMo (gpt-5.6-sol)","description":"CONCLUDED: mem0-oss Haiku shim worked (docker llm=anthropic), but the Claude OAuth token is a personal subscription → 23x 429 rate-limits → ~8h ETA + burns user quota. STOPPED to protect quota. Comparator falls back to mem0 published gpt-5 ref (91.0/91.56/70.1/50.5).","activeForm":"Running mem0-oss matched lane","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"17","subject":"Run eg BEAM 1M/10M (mem0 config) on mem0 harness","description":"DONE: eg BEAM 1M = 0.494/57.0% vs mem0 published 0.641/70.1% (eg loses −13pts; weak on knowledge_update/contradiction/temporal = consolidation). Speed: 7.3min deterministic ingest, 0 LLM calls vs mem0 ~30k/tier. Config verified fair (gpt-5, top_k 200). BEAM 10M SKIPPED per user (too costly, would confirm bigger loss).","activeForm":"Running eg BEAM 1M/10M","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"18","subject":"Fix + complete the 8-arm graphmark run (supermemory)","description":"SUPERSEDED, not finished. The sealed graphify-parity 8-arm harness jammed on letta for 14+ hours and produced nothing (poller bgfktrera: 83 polls of arms_built=letta only, then blank). Replaced by the mem0-harness field run, which has 3 complete arms (eg 92.73, mem0 87.40, cognee 79.09) with per-category breakdowns and measured timings, plus letta working in-process. Track B stays parked; document as the prior attempt in the release writeup.","activeForm":"Fixing + completing the 8-arm run","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"19","subject":"Build deterministic consolidation prototype (Phase A)","description":"DONE + unit-tested: consolidate.py (717 LOC, pure deterministic 0-LLM/0-net) = timeline + rule-based supersession (Honda→Tesla verified) + dedup/alias → writes _timeline/_current_facts/_superseded.md into eg corpus. entire_client.py env-gated EG_CONSOLIDATE (byte-identical when off, backup made). Unit test PASS + byte-identical replay. A/B script ~/eg_consolidate_ab.sh gated on /tmp/terra_done, NOT launched. NEXT: run A/B after terra.","activeForm":"Building consolidation prototype","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"20","subject":"Build + test consolidation v2 (user_profile, pollution-free)","description":"WORKS (first positive lever). v2 = consolidated facts via user_profile prompt section (retrieval byte-identical, NO pollution). gpt-5 LME: 88.4→89.4 (+1.0); temporal +3.0, multi-session +1.5, knowledge-update +1.3 ALL UP; single-session regressed (pref -3.3, assist -1.8 = the profile distracts single-session Qs). Diagnosis confirmed: v1's problem was pollution not content. Closes mem0 gap -2.6→-1.6. NEXT: query-gate the profile to stop single-session leak → could hit +2-3.","activeForm":"Building + testing consolidation v2","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"21","subject":"Instrument timing/cost columns in all benchmark tables","description":"DONE. Cost/time captured for every arm: build/history (eg 0.55s, mem0 ~131s, letta 346s, cognee 457s, supermemory 1538s, graphiti 4464s + ~2000 LLM calls), corpus ingest (eg 8.08s vs mem0 20471s = 2533x), end-to-end micro-run (eg 5s vs cognee 504s vs mem0 1522s = ~300x), query p50/p95, LLM-calls-per-history (eg=0), and the LME feasibility table (per-unit cost x 500: eg ~5min vs mem0 18h, letta 48h, cognee 63h, supermemory 213h, graphiti 620h). All in deliverable/RESULTS.md §5 and MEMORY-BENCH-DELIVERABLE.md §4, measured-vs-reconstructed labelled, contended timings excluded.","activeForm":"Instrumenting timing/cost capture across field arms","owner":"field-port-agent","status":"completed","blocks":["22"],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"22","subject":"Release-prep: verify eg score reproduces, push, docs, cleanup both repos","description":"After all runs complete: (1) re-verify eg LME score reproduces at 95.07 mean from the shipped code path (no drift); (2) push all changes to entire-graph + graphmark; (3) update READMEs/docs with the fair methodology, accuracy+time tables, reproduction instructions; (4) clean both repos (remove scratch/dead files, backups, disabled guards); (5) make fully release-ready. Blocked until field run + Track A finish. Confirm with user before any push.","activeForm":"Preparing repos for release","status":"pending","blocks":[],"blockedBy":["21","14"]},{"id":"23","subject":"Diagnose graphiti near-zero smoke before publishing any row","description":"gr_smoke scored 0/5 and 1/5 (0-20%). Near-zero for a real product = almost certainly a broken port (empty retrieved context, neo4j group_id/namespace mismatch between write and read, wrong search API, or silently-swallowed ingest exceptions). Diagnose before quoting ANY graphiti number. If it cannot be made to retrieve, DROP the arm with documented reason (\"could not achieve working port; not a statement about graphiti quality\"). Same plausibility standard applies to supermemory and every other arm.","activeForm":"Diagnosing graphiti near-zero smoke","owner":"field-port-agent","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"24","subject":"Resolve cognee extractor provenance (terra vs gpt-5 default)","description":"RESOLVED DEFINITIVELY. Cognee's preserved per-call request payloads (659 files at /tmp/cognee_field_loco2_*/.{build,search}_*.req.json) for the exact run producing the banked 79.09% (byte-identical to locomo_results_20260813_061507.json) show llm_model = azure_ai/gpt-5.6-terra in 659/659. Correct fairness-spine extractor confirmed; no caveat needed. NOTE: COGNEE_LLM_MODEL still defaults to azure_ai/gpt-5 for FUTURE launches without an inline override — that default is what killed two LME attempts (LLMAPIKeyNotSetError crashing the whole asyncio.gather silently). Always set it explicitly.","activeForm":"Resolving cognee extractor provenance","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"25","subject":"Cognee LoCoMo was corrupt — re-run and re-test the headline","description":"RESOLVED. Corrected cognee LoCoMo = 92.86% (1430/1540) vs eg 92.73% (1428/1540). McNemar exact p=0.93; bootstrap 95% CI on (eg-cognee) = [-1.49,+1.23]pp, includes 0 → STATISTICALLY INDISTINGUISHABLE. eg does NOT win LoCoMo; it ties cognee. n=529 subset flips the order (eg 92.25 vs cognee 91.68), confirming a tie. Original 79.09% was corrupted by the empty-buffer bug (301/1540 questions). eg's remaining decisive wins: LME 95.07 vs mem0-OSS 82.2, and cost (0.55s vs 457s/history; cognee cannot economically run LME at n=500).","activeForm":"Re-running cognee LoCoMo and re-testing the headline","owner":"field-agent-2","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"26","subject":"Independent adversarial fairness audit of the field comparison","description":"AUDIT COMPLETE — found 8 findings, 6 UNFAIR. SEVERE: (F1) mem0 ran effective top_k=20 not 200 on BOTH benchmarks — client sends `limit`, mem0 server expects `top_k`, Pydantic drops it, default 20; proven by mem0 returning exactly 20 items on 500/500 LME + 1540/1540 LoCoMo; eg got 124x more context on LME. (F2) eg's LME arm read raw dataset corpus off disk uncapped via EG_SESSION_EXPAND=2/CAP=0 → 590K chars/question ≈ whole haystack, worth +4.80pp, no competitor path. (F3) eg-only answerer prompt block EG_ANSWER_ENUM, +0.47pp. (F4) eg-only \"## User Profile\" section on 498/500 questions, architecturally exclusive. (F5) eg's 95.07 = top of 17-run sweep on the published test set; untuned = 89.80 vs mem0 82.2. (F6) empty-buffer fix reached only cognee's number; supermemory/letta scores produced by the defective client; eg+mem0 ran without the retry wrapper. (F7) supermemory's 77.60 hides 14.4% zero-retrieval (88.48% on the rest). (F8) n=529 subset worth +0.69pp to eg relative to cognee. SURVIVES: LoCoMo eg 92.73 vs cognee 92.86 tie — both untuned, identical spine, forensics re-verified independently, cognee got 3.4x eg's context.","activeForm":"Running independent adversarial fairness audit","owner":"fairness-auditor","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"27","subject":"GATE: complete all fixes, then STOP for user review before launching matrix","description":"DONE. All fixes applied+verified (top_k durable across container rebuild; FAIR_MODE=1 hard-exits on arm-asymmetric settings incl. --user-profile CLI flag; runmeta.py captures env/argv/code-md5s; buffer-invariant raises in all 5 clients; entire-graph PATH symlink). FAIR-CONFIG.md written (md5 0300d7e5..., 373 lines). User reviewed and approved the full matrix; it ran. Final results in deliverable/RESULTS.md (184 lines, synced to graph-bench-results/RESULTS-MEMORY-BENCH.md).","activeForm":"Completing fixes and preparing review package","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"28","subject":"Verified plan for eg to beat all on LoCoMo by 0.5pt (or prove the ceiling)","description":"Workflow wn10dtajp running: 4 parallel angles (byte-budget cap, index granularity, the 50 answerer-failures, LME path) → each attacked by 2 independent skeptics (fairness + validity/effect-size) → synthesized into one ranked plan with protocol and honest reachability verdict. Targets: LoCoMo >=93.94, LME 95. Gap is 11 multi-hop questions. Leading lever: --max-context-bytes 24576→65536 (+47% units). Barred: corpus reads, eg-only prompts, test-set sweeping. Falsified: --deep, --head, chrono-order.","activeForm":"Developing verified plan to beat all on LoCoMo","status":"pending","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"29","subject":"eg's own harness cap: --max-context-bytes truncating retrieval by 47%","description":"REFUTED. The adapter passes --max-context-bytes 100_000_000 (entire_client.py:117), not the CLI fallback 24576. Measured: 24576→19.5 units/4,388 chars; 65536→32.0/24,320; 131072→32.0/24,527; 100M→32.0/24,527. eg already retrieves one hit from every session in real runs; there is nothing to recover. My earlier \"eg truncated to 19/4 units\" claim measured a configuration the harness never uses — retracted. Superseded by the real lever: multi-resolution (turn+session) indexing, +2.21pt.","activeForm":"Testing eg's max-context-bytes cap","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"30","subject":"Rotate exposed credentials (Azure + Fireworks)","description":"Two live secrets were read into subagent process environments this session. AZURE_AI_API_KEY (VM2 ~/.azenv, len=84, sha256=cd7418253f37, tail=...ktWR) and FIREWORKS_API_KEY (VM2 ~/memarms/run.env, len=25, sha256=275314134e96, tail=...AZev). EMBEDDING_API_KEY (len=13, tail=...auth) appears to be a no-auth placeholder. VM1 ~/.azure_env uses export-style syntax — read directly. Rotating will require updating ~/.azenv on VM2, ~/.azure_env on VM1, and run.env before further runs.","activeForm":"Rotating exposed credentials","status":"pending","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"31","subject":"Promote eg multi-resolution indexing to official harness + confirm 94.74","description":"Winning config: EG_INGEST_GRANULARITY=turn+session (multi-resolution / parent-document chunking) — writes both a per-turn doc and the whole-session doc from the same add() payloads. Measured in ~/plan_harness: eg 92.53 base → 94.74 hybrid (n=1540, same-window paired, CI [+1.17,+3.25], p=6e-5, 0 drops, every category up). Beats target 93.94 by +0.80, mem0 93.44 by +1.30, cognee 92.86 by +1.88. Fair: ingest-side only, 0 LLM calls, question-blind, no prompt/answerer/judge/top_k change, no dataset reads, default path byte-identical (sha256 verified). Cost: index 0.20s→0.63s, search 242ms→826ms. TO CLOSE: (1) port config into ~/mem0harness as an official field_ run, (2) 3-arm same-window run mem0+eg_base+eg_hyb to validate the margin vs mem0 (both prior mem0 pairings corrupted by a duplicate-launch bug), (3) 2-3 replicates for a drift-robust CI.","activeForm":"Promoting multi-resolution config and confirming 94.74","status":"pending","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"32","subject":"Test multi-resolution indexing on LongMemEval (target ≥94.9)","description":"Does EG_INGEST_GRANULARITY=turn+session transfer from LoCoMo (+2.21) to LME? LME histories have 43-57 sessions vs LoCoMo's 29, so the parent-document effect could be larger. Baseline eg LME 89.80 (n=500, atomic, untuned). Targets: mem0-OSS fair 87.20 (already beaten by +2.60); mem0 PUBLISHED managed 94.4 → eg needs ≥94.9, must be labelled cross-config since managed is a different product tier and not reproducible. Also audit whether eg95_bm25c8=91.60 is fair (BM25 fusion is eg's own retrieval; check no corpus reads, no eg-only prompt/profile, not test-set-selected) and whether it stacks with multi-res — report levers separately. Design: one run each, paired same-window, no replicates (F5 symmetry). Barred: EG_SESSION_EXPAND corpus reads, EG_ANSWER_ENUM, user_profile, solhyb_* configs.","activeForm":"Testing multi-resolution on LongMemEval","status":"pending","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]}],"itemCount":32},"type":"attachment","uuid":"13d85332-ed90-445d-86fc-c30912a60f1a","timestamp":"2026-08-17T01:00:29.806Z","session_id":"fe41fb4b-5221-41ce-afce-6a9fa3dade0c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"27642e0f-a981-4143-aea0-6f4f8cb34d37","version":"2.1.226","gitBranch":"main","slug":"structured-meandering-origami"}
