{"parentUuid":"01b3b6f8-df22-48bf-a096-e0002c0c15e2","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"task_reminder","content":[{"id":"1","subject":"Decide #82↔#84 merge order + schema-bump question","description":"Workflow wf_8b9d1d00-a24 investigating: PR84 scope/results, PR82 head live-repro of #sig ID churn, pinned-symbol-ID sweep (cmm/entire-brain/p0p1), agentGuide gap. On completion: synthesize, post decision in AGENT-COMMS.md (which PR lands first; whether ID contract must be held / schema-version bump needed before #82 merges).","activeForm":"Deciding #82↔#84 merge order","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"2","subject":"Adversarially verify PR #84 prose-memory/LOCOMO numbers before merge","description":"DONE 2026-08-07 (wf_0bc841c9-645, offline $0): arithmetic ALL_CONFIRMED 8/8 bit-for-bit; integrity ISSUES_FOUND — cmm null arm (24-byte empty context all 1050 cells), full set 10% tune-overlapped (quote holdout 0.756/0.900 beside full), holdout scored 4x across lineage, config.json provenance incomplete. Entire-vs-Graphify +0.1648 [0.1034,0.2146] survives fairness audit. Merge conditions in MemoryNotes §4.","activeForm":"Verifying PR #84 LOCOMO numbers","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"3","subject":"Guard shipped agentGuide const (internal/cli/agents.go)","description":"DONE: PR #87 (test/agent-guide-const-parity, commit 01529ca) — checkGuideClaims(t, origin, source) extracted, TestAgentGuideConstMatchesFlagRegistry added. CRITICAL improvement over plan: naive version was VACUOUS (const yields 0 flag claims — it uses indented code blocks, not fences); agent mutation-tested, taught parser indented blocks (guideIndentedCodeRE, no-op for AGENTS.md), const now yields 9 commands + 20 flags and mutations fail. All tests+vet green. Awaiting review/merge.","activeForm":"Guarding shipped agentGuide","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"4","subject":"Restore gcloud auth for graphbench-c access","description":"RESOLVED 2026-08-07: user ran gcloud auth login (suhaan@entire.io, project graph-benchmarks-504800). Verified: graphbench-a/b/c all RUNNING (c4-standard-32, us-east1-b). NOTE: graphbench-d does NOT exist despite comms calling it \"bare/free\" — will need creating if used for the full run.","activeForm":"Waiting on gcloud reauth","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"5","subject":"Write comp.md — memory competitive landscape","description":"Assemble /Users/suhaan/devenv/comp.md: competitor table (mem0, cmm, graphify, cognee, supermemory, letta, +zep/graphiti for the LOCOMO-dispute context) with GH links + all published benchmark claims (source-checked); our measured status against each on memory benches; section on how the graphmark memory/prose-memory suite works. Inputs: workflow wf_8343ced9-b55 (research) + wf_8b9d1d00-a24 (PR84 claimed numbers).","activeForm":"Writing comp.md","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"6","subject":"Build + verify competitor memory arms and BEAM, then plan full comparison","description":"DONE: 5 arms + BEAM built, adversarially verified (6/6 PASS_WITH_FIXES), ALL 35 verifier fixes applied (11 integrator + 24 rebase agent, 0 rejected), merged with post-cleanup graphmark main via correct 3-way (squash-merge ancestry handled), locator-v3 byte-intact proven, native-packing decision documented in RUN-PLAN §6.2, 518 tests + 5 smokes + BEAM dry-run green. Final SHA 644a430b, memarms/comp-arms-v1, not pushed. BEAM judge int-truncation defect (0.5→0, binary metric) documented upstream-facing.","activeForm":"Building competitor memory arms","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"7","subject":"Execute the full 8-arm field comparison (approved)","description":"APPROVED run. TOPOLOGY RESOLVED (source-proven): VM phases need NO claude/anthropic (probe confined to memory-score; memory arms' MCP even strips the token). Freeze sealed ALL-VM paths incl. a Linux claude binary on f → memory-score runs ON f