{"parentUuid":"7c74ab2d-7b61-435a-a585-4602a6765db8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce7d2vRbFA4hSBhdkQtay","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"gofmt clean, vet clean, **2,725 tests passed**. Committing."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":649,"cache_read_input_tokens":393309,"output_tokens":1720,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":649,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1720,"cache_read_input_tokens":393309,"cache_creation_input_tokens":649,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":649},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce7d2ZcCeDqV3R5Zz2WNj","type":"assistant","uuid":"d5af9ef9-46ff-48ec-bdae-eedab265cb47","timestamp":"2026-08-17T03:37:12.588Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"fe41fb4b-5221-41ce-afce-6a9fa3dade0c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/eg-multires","sessionId":"27642e0f-a981-4143-aea0-6f4f8cb34d37","version":"2.1.226","gitBranch":"main","slug":"structured-meandering-origami"}
{"parentUuid":"d5af9ef9-46ff-48ec-bdae-eedab265cb47","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce7d2vRbFA4hSBhdkQtay","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RqVSB9hnHVnwdTanAJgGfh","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/eg-multires\ngit status --short\ngit add -A\ngit -c user.email=\"suhaanthayyil0@gmail.com\" -c user.name=\"Suhaan Thayyil\" commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nfix(search): keep section units off code, keep results score-ordered\n\nAddresses the seven review findings on #104.\n\nSection units leaked into code results. The corpus gate is counted over the\nwhole matched path mix, so a docs-heavy repository opens it while still\ncontaining source files, and every candidate was then keyed by symbol. A source\nfile has many symbols, so each contributed many units -- and since one region\nper unit is what enforces MaxRegionsPerFile for code, removing the rule\nsilently uncapped it. Section keying and passage planning are now restricted to\ncandidates whose own path is a document, so a code region keeps falling back to\nits file. Measured on 20 .md + 3 .go at --top-k 30: ranked regions of one .go\nfile 2 -> 1.\n\nPromoted results broke the descending-score ordering of results[]. A promotion\ncarries its parent's score, so appending it left a high-scoring passage behind\nevery low-scoring parent and a consumer taking \"top 20 by score\" got a\ndifferent set than the first 20 entries. results[] is now re-sorted stably, so\na promotion settles beside its parent and the array is monotone again. Set\nmembership is untouched: promotion stays strictly additive.\n\nSection results nested inside a higher-ranked same-file window reprinted their\ntext. dropSelectedProsePassages keeps the ranked regions disjoint as SELECTED,\nbut allocateSearchSnippets then grows them -- an 80-line prose head window\nswallows the sections that legitimately won their own slots -- and nothing\nre-checked afterwards. Containment is now resolved after growth and before\npromotion, so the freed slots are spent on regions the payload does not already\nshow.\n\nThe promotion fitter re-serialized the whole result set once per candidate\ncount. Serialized size is strictly increasing in count, so the largest fitting\ncount is found by bisection instead: ~log2(n) serializations rather than n. A\nzero budget now applies every planned promotion directly rather than looping.\n\nSingleResolution's doc comment claimed it restored \"one result per file\". It\ndoes not on its own -- promotion and section ranking are independent knobs, and\nreproducing the previous payload needs both flags. Comment corrected rather\nthan behaviour changed, since turning off promotion while keeping section\nranking is a real configuration.\n\nThe scale guard covered only the non-default path: proseScaleCandidates emits\none candidate per file, so section units are a no-op there whichever way the\nflag is passed. Adds a fixture with real sections plus a linearity guard and\nbenchmark on the default path (200 files x 20 sections: 23,639 allocs, 4.4 MB).\n\nThe help text presented section ranking and multi-resolution as alternatives.\nThey stack -- a headed document can be ranked by section and still have spare\nslots filled with promoted passages.\n\nVerified: code-search payloads byte-identical across 21 query/top-k pairs\n(latency telemetry excluded). On a LoCoMo-shaped corpus the retrieved set and\nsnippet bytes are identical at every budget tested; only the order changes.\nEOF\necho \"--- committed ---\"; git log --oneline -1; git status --short | head -3","description":"Commit the review fixes","timeout":300000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":649,"cache_read_input_tokens":393309,"output_tokens":1720,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":649,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1720,"cache_read_input_tokens":393309,"cache_creation_input_tokens":649,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":649},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce7d2ZcCeDqV3R5Zz2WNj","type":"assistant","uuid":"7a168d2e-d2b9-41c6-8796-3329e6756170","timestamp":"2026-08-17T03:37:27.821Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"fe41fb4b-5221-41ce-afce-6a9fa3dade0c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/eg-multires","sessionId":"27642e0f-a981-4143-aea0-6f4f8cb34d37","version":"2.1.226","gitBranch":"main","slug":"structured-meandering-origami"}
{"parentUuid":"7a168d2e-d2b9-41c6-8796-3329e6756170","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"505f5b2a-6f54-4004-9ada-8e02163a6b4a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RqVSB9hnHVnwdTanAJgGfh","type":"tool_result","content":" M internal/cli/help.go\n M internal/sem/search.go\n M internal/sem/search_multi_resolution.go\n M internal/sem/search_multi_resolution_test.go\n M internal/sem/search_prose_parent.go\n M internal/sem/search_prose_session_test.go\n--- committed ---\n7ef28b9 fix(search): keep section units off code, keep results score-ordered","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"f03bfe35-26c3-411e-a760-87a052d44c9e","timestamp":"2026-08-17T03:37:48.080Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":" M internal/cli/help.go\n M internal/sem/search.go\n M internal/sem/search_multi_resolution.go\n M internal/sem/search_multi_resolution_test.go\n M internal/sem/search_prose_parent.go\n M internal/sem/search_prose_session_test.go\n--- committed ---\n7ef28b9 fix(search): keep section units off code, keep results score-ordered","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7a168d2e-d2b9-41c6-8796-3329e6756170","session_id":"fe41fb4b-5221-41ce-afce-6a9fa3dade0c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/eg-multires","sessionId":"27642e0f-a981-4143-aea0-6f4f8cb34d37","version":"2.1.226","gitBranch":"main","slug":"structured-meandering-origami"}
{"parentUuid":"f03bfe35-26c3-411e-a760-87a052d44c9e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce7d6bConYVaBxR7w5gCm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Benchmarks: the evidence is unchanged, only the ordering is.** I checked this specifically before committing, because two of the seven fixes touch prose retrieval and prose retrieval *is* what LoCoMo measures.\n\nOn a LoCoMo-shaped corpus (19 sessions × 24 turns, `top_k=200`):\n\n| budget | results | set identical | snippet chars |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 24,576 | 19 → 19 | yes | 14,662 → 14,662 |\n| 65,536 | 19 → 19 | yes | 14,662 → 14,662 |\n| 262,144 | 200 → 200 | yes | 32,404 → 32,404 |\n\nZero divergence at every budget — the answerer receives byte-for-byte the same evidence. The only change is the order within `results[]`, which is now score-monotone (that was the bug). So recall is provably unchanged and 94.74 should reproduce, but I want to be exact: *should*, not *does*. Reordering identical evidence can still move a reader's answer through position effects, and I can't re-run to confirm because gcloud auth expired.\n\n## The seven findings, all addressed\n\n**Section units leaked into code.** The gate counts the whole path mix, so a docs-heavy repo opens it while still holding `.go` files — which then got keyed by symbol, and since one-region-per-unit is what enforces `MaxRegionsPerFile`, that silently uncapped it. Section keying *and* passage planning are now restricted to document paths. Measured on 20 `.md` + 3 `.go`: ranked regions of one `.go` file **2 → 1**.\n\n**Score ordering broken.** Promotions inherit the parent's score and were appended, so a high-scoring passage sat behind every low-scoring parent. Now stably re-sorted — a promotion settles beside its parent, membership untouched, so promotion stays strictly additive.\n\n**Nested snippets reprinted text.** Dedup ran on spans *as selected*; `allocateSearchSnippets` then grew them and nothing re-checked. Containment now resolves after growth and **before** promotion, so freed slots go to regions not already shown. Contained pairs **1 → 0**.\n\n**Fitter re-serialized per candidate count** → bisection, ~log2(n) instead of n.\n\n**`SingleResolution` comment** corrected rather than behavior changed — turning off promotion while keeping section ranking is a real configuration.\n\n**Scale guard** now has a real-sections fixture on the default path (200 files × 20 sections: 23,639 allocs / 4.4 MB — matching the reviewer's 23,219 / 4.4 MB).\n\n**Help text** now says the two levers stack.\n\nGate: gofmt clean, vet clean, **2,725 tests pass**, and code-search payloads byte-identical across 21 query/top-k pairs. One caught false alarm along the way — my first parity check showed 0/10 identical, which turned out to be latency telemetry, not behavior.\n\nCommitted as `7ef28b9`, **not pushed**. Want me to push and post replies to the seven review threads?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1860,"cache_read_input_tokens":393958,"output_tokens":1037,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1860,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1037,"cache_read_input_tokens":393958,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1860,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1860},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce7d6GVR4b4TcVUyCLYMf","type":"assistant","uuid":"5701717e-a07a-4161-9096-d2844a417ab5","timestamp":"2026-08-17T03:38:07.567Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"fe41fb4b-5221-41ce-afce-6a9fa3dade0c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/eg-multires","sessionId":"27642e0f-a981-4143-aea0-6f4f8cb34d37","version":"2.1.226","g